  "result": {
    "summary": "The coach observes a replay where the controlled hero (Ranger) walks all the way back to base before activating their town scroll (teleport). The coach instructs that the agent should activate town scroll while out in the field (in lane or river) when low on health rather than walking back to base.\n\nThis coverage review adds missing execution and goal layer specifications omitted in the first pass. While the draft identified the skill selection rule to use the town scroll in the field when low on health, it lacked the execution-level channel controller needed to prevent input cancellation during the 3.0-second cast time, as well as the explicit goal prioritization governing field retreat. It also identifies a crucial mechanic ambiguity regarding whether town scrolls function as a fixed base recall or targetable structure teleport.",
